{"cache_mechanism_finding":{"boundary_condition_not_proven":"This experiment used a single whole-tensor SET_TENSOR call (offset=0, one contiguous chunk). It does not prove (and does not assume) the same result for a tensor whose assignment is fragmented into multiple (offset, size) sub-ranges by llama.cpp's own runtime tensor-split logic (e.g. proportional multi-device memory splitting); reproducing the exact chunk boundaries needed to pre-stage such a tensor is left as an explicit open boundary, not claimed to work.","case_classification":"C","case_classification_meaning":"existing cache can consume pre-staged backing with a bounded external adapter, no llama.cpp modification","cold_exceeded_hash_threshold":true,"durable_cache_reuse_suppresses_retransmission":true,"legal_non_runtime_modifying_seam_exists":true,"measured":{"cold_set_phase_bytes_sent":12583546,"prestaged_set_phase_bytes_sent":321,"truncated_get_exit_code":2,"warm_restart_set_phase_bytes_sent":321,"wrong_content_get_exit_code":2},"non_claim_fnv1a_is_not_inferswarm_trust_authority":"The upstream FNV-1a filename is a 64-bit non-cryptographic dedup key the pinned server trusts blindly on read (rpc_server::get_cached_file never re-hashes the file it loads). Phases D and E mechanically prove this: wrong content and truncated content are both served as a 'hit' without detection. Any adapter that populates this cache from InferSwarm-verified local backing MUST perform InferSwarm's own SHA-256/provenance verification before writing to the cache path -- the FNV-1a name is never sufficient and is never treated as InferSwarm trust authority.","pinned_llama_cpp_commit":"b29c606e28a01b1bc8c1351026a0fa6e616bf6c4","prestaged_verified_backing_consumed_without_prior_network_pass":true,"requires_external_provenance_verification_before_cache_population":true,"schema":"inferswarm.issue200.rpc-cache-mechanical-finding/1","upstream_cache_is_fail_open_on_wrong_or_truncated_content":true},"compact_source_policy_seam_pass":true,"execution_environment_note":{"note":"The Phase-1..4 session's SSH BatchMode probe to inferswarm01 was rejected for lack of a usable credential, which is why Phase 5 was handed off rather than run then. The Phase-5 session (2026-09-16) held a usable credential and executed the bounded physical comparison; the retained physical evidence, not this note, is the authority for what it proved.","phase4_session_fleet_authorized":false,"phase5_session_fleet_authorized":true,"schema":"inferswarm.issue200.execution-environment-note/2"},"incomplete":false,"phase4_launch_configuration_finding":{"client_process_receives_model_path_argument":true,"evidence_source":"scripts/issue195_v2_launch.py","finding":"In the exact accepted R8-D v2 launch configuration, the client llama-server process is the only process given a model path; every ggml-rpc-server backend process is launched with only -H/-p/-d, no model path and no -c/--cache flag. This narrow fact is scoped to this one launch configuration. It does not, by itself, establish whether the pinned ggml-rpc runtime has any participant-local-backing seam -- that broader question is answered separately and correctly by cache_mechanism_finding, not by this fact.","pinned_llama_cpp_commit":"b29c606e28a01b1bc8c1351026a0fa6e616bf6c4","retraction_note":"An earlier revision of this reducer used this launch-configuration fact alone to conclude 'the RPC backend process has no independent model-loading capability and no seam to consume a participant-local verified artifact for its assigned tensors without the client retransmitting those exact bytes over the wire' and emitted R8F_RUNTIME_LOCAL_BACKING_PREREQUISITE on that basis. That conclusion did not inspect the pinned ggml-rpc-server's local-cache implementation (tools/rpc/rpc-server.cpp, ggml/src/ggml-rpc/ggml-rpc.cpp) at all and is retracted. It is superseded by cache_mechanism_finding, which mechanically tested that seam directly against the pinned binary.","rpc_backend_process_receives_cache_flag":false,"rpc_backend_process_receives_model_path_argument":false,"schema":"inferswarm.issue200.phase4-finding/2"},"physical_phase5_evidence_status":{"derived":{"accepted_model_authority":{"authority_path":"docs/investigations/qwen38-flash-next-r8-d-v2/evidence/split-identity/split-rehash.json","members":[{"bytes":10946624,"file":"Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-IQ1_S-00001-of-00003.gguf","sha256":"88a1420825a9304063e882ada29d438263617f51ac8923d438d927496693bafd"},{"bytes":49990818368,"file":"Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-IQ1_S-00002-of-00003.gguf","sha256":"3a62e35bbf9add4733bd1438ebd3a67649d5edd6cb0e72bb78e33c913992b2b6"},{"bytes":22544696352,"file":"Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-UD-IQ1_S-00003-of-00003.gguf","sha256":"0e25ceaeb89b8a80aa973c6c0c7448943682f7408c2855b2ebd016b7643a861a"}],"total_bytes":72546461344},"identities":{"materialization_identity":"sha256:c85639e754002df55607a4971a574a4c7e76f09f6075b2df526c13bd68e082b7","participant_requirements_identity":"sha256:4c072eb4680615706b88e8a4643db7491930c8a3d98182eb27b4b7b089af066c","placement_identity":"sha256:971f203a00ae25b625bdb9505b00a1c6cd7ca06c69f500acdcd88d66c23a5a4b","required_state_identity":"sha256:c8a2c425a1aff45d8a5097960095d079cd3b48309bb0dcfd6d57dbb7b5fba13d"},"network":{"cold_remote":{"immutable_payload":10813440,"payload_identities":[{"length":10813440,"observation_id":"set-blk.24.attn_gate.weight","offset":848968992,"order":1,"participant":"inferswarm04","sha256":"1c0284d8b85f4966e2dd1990271f3bc470667c11041d5d084be1ca511080f5f4"}],"rpc_control":97255,"total":10910695},"local_verified":{"immutable_payload":0,"payload_identities":[],"rpc_control":96942,"total":96942},"repeat_local_verified":{"immutable_payload":0,"payload_identities":[],"rpc_control":96942,"total":96942}},"participants":["inferswarm04"],"payload_boundaries":[{"fnv1a_cache_key":"bbc9ae6a1038b6a6","length":10813440,"observation_id":"set-blk.24.attn_gate.weight","offset":848968992,"order":1,"participant":"inferswarm04","sha256":"1c0284d8b85f4966e2dd199